      "summary": "",
      "body": "Panmnesia boosts CXL scale with fabric switching. Meta repurposes old DRAM with CXL\nPanmnesia is pushing ahead with advancing combined CXL and UAL/Ethernet technology by sampling a fusion chip bringing PCIe and CXL together as a stage towards CXL/UAL unification, while Meta is using CXL to add old DRAM to new servers, boost their DRAM capacity and make them go faster.\nPanmnesia is a Korean fabless, semiconductor company designing CXL controllers and switches. CXL (Computer eXpress Link) is the extension of the PCIe bus outside a server’s chassis, initially based on the PCIe 5.0 standard, and absorbing the PCIe gen 6 and 7 standards.\nMyoungsoo Jung, CEO of Panmnesia, said: “There has been a perception that putting a switch between the CPU and devices makes it hard to meet the memory-access latency these systems expect, so directly attached MHDs (Multi-Headed Devices) stayed the norm even though they were harder to scale. Our work shows this is not an inherent limit of CXL or CXL switche",
